# Ask the recognizer to judge the scene at specific future instants.
#
# The times are the request, not the images. The recognizer subscribes to the
# cameras itself and captures at the scheduled instants; the manager sends
# only when and what to look for.
#
# It is built this way because the capture instant is load-bearing. The
# probes were trained on frames at fixed offsets from a boundary -- mat at
# +3/12/21 frames after a flip run begins, tray at +8/18/28 after the gripper
# opens -- and a verdict from a different instant judges a scene the probe
# never saw. Shipping images in the request would also put three 640x480
# frames into a service call at a boundary the control loop is crossing.

# See RecognitionVerdict for the purposes. The probe follows from it:
# start and flip use `mat`, place uses `tray`.
uint8 purpose

# Capture offsets from `reference`, in seconds. The manager converts the
# recognizer config's frame offsets using the control fps, so the one place
# that knows the fps is the one that owns it.
float32[] offsets_s

# Instant the offsets are measured from -- the boundary itself (the release,
# the flip transition, the episode start). Zero means "now, as the recognizer
# receives this". Scheduling off a stamp the manager chose, rather than off
# arrival, keeps the queueing delay out of the capture times.
builtin_interfaces/Time reference

# Drop any captures still pending from earlier requests before scheduling
# these. Set on a replan: verdicts for a subtask the plan has abandoned
# arrive late and would be applied to the wrong boundary.
bool cancel_pending
---
# False when no recognizer model is loaded, or when an offset has already
# passed by more than the recognizer's tolerance. The manager runs without
# verification in that case rather than waiting for a verdict that is not
# coming.
bool success
string message

# Echoed into every resulting RecognitionVerdict.
uint32 request_id

# How many captures were actually scheduled. The manager aggregates after
# this many verdicts arrive.
uint8 scheduled
